{
    "background_story": "Promise was a brilliant linguist with a passion for languages. Growing up in a multicultural community, she was exposed to various tongues from a young age. By the time she was 16, Promise was fluent in five languages, including Mandarin, Arabic, Spanish, French, and English. Her fascination with language led her to pursue a degree in linguistics, where she excelled in her studies. After college, Promise worked as a translator for the United Nations, using her skills to facilitate communication between world leaders. Her polyglot abilities allowed her to connect with people from diverse backgrounds, fostering global understanding and cooperation. Promise's love for languages took her to over 20 countries, where she immersed herself in local cultures and learned even more dialects. Her remarkable talent earned her the nickname 'The Language Ambassador'.",
